# The vendored linguist profile is a derived file whose whole value as a
# reviewable artifact is that regenerating it at the same upstream commit
# produces byte-identical output. `scripts/refresh_linguist.py` writes it with
# LF; this repository is checked out under `core.autocrlf=true` and carries no
# other .gitattributes, so without this line git hands the file back with CRLF
# on the next checkout and every future refresh diff is the entire file.
#
# Scoped deliberately to this one path. A repo-wide `*.json text eol=lf` would
# renormalize the existing profiles/extractors.json, which is checked out with
# CRLF today and is nobody's business here.
tools/legacylift_search/src/legacylift_search/profiles/linguist.json text eol=lf

# The vendored web fonts under docs/legacylift-v4-overview/ are binary. Git's
# content heuristic happens to classify them correctly today, but under this
# repository's `core.autocrlf=true` an unspecified attribute leaves that to a
# guess -- and a woff2 that gets CRLF-normalized on checkout is a silently
# broken font on someone else's clone. Pin it rather than rely on the guess.
docs/legacylift-v4-overview/assets/fonts/*.woff2 binary
